This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old (or bad) ideas that may be
present.

[1]: The Helm of Brilliance should also be a light source while worn
with radius equal to the current enchantment. If the enchantment is
negative, it should reduce the radius of light from your other light
sources, but naturally not to less than zero. -azgor

[2]: Decapitating medusa should create a corpse and a head. When the
head is wielded, all non stoning resistant non-sightless monsters in
your line of sight should be stoned. It should be as perishable as a
cockatrice corpse. This is not imbalancing as it would be very hard to
get this item. You would need to be blind or stoning resistant to wield
the head this way. Be sure to take it to the bigroom. -azgor

[3]: Trapdoors should always come out in the same place, if that's
codeable. It makes sense. -ekiM

[4]: Acid resistance is meaningless.  Add a couple monsters (say, a
purple S) that spit acid for 4d10 or something, so that acid resistance
might be worth considering -ekiM

[5]: Zapping wands of digging <: A way to make holes in the ceiling,
such that you can levitate up through them. -workimer

[6]: If teleporting monsters can't make it to the upstair, they
teleport to the downstair. If they can't make it there, they teleport a
long way from you to heal up. They're supposed to be supreme evil
opponents, not klutzes who get outfoxed by a boulder on their escape
route. There might have to be a longer tele-timeout to balance this.
-ekiM

[7]: fire should turn a clay golem into a stone or glass (?) golem (per
rng) -mathx
[8]: fire shold not affect glass golems -mathx

[9]: Force bolt/striking should do extra damage to stone golems, as
statues are destroyed easily with the spell/wand. -Grunt

[10]: #chatting with proper named monsters as a tourist should have a
chance of receiving an autograph from that monster or a message stating
"Foo looks at you funny."  Multiple failed requests from the monster
should give the message "You seem to have pestered the foo too much.."
and the player should gain aggravate monster for a few hundred turns.
-aristotle73

[11]: Innumerate conduct. An option. 'One, two, many'. For example - a)
Many arrows. b) blessed +lots silver dragon scale mail. -SpeedEvil

[12]: If you ignite some scrolls, their magic energy would be released
and appropriate effects would happen.  (Death field for a scroll of
genocide?) -Grunt

[13]: Ochre(?) Dragons with a sickness breath attack. Ochre Dragon
Scale mail provides sickness reistsance (too powerful? maybe it
converts the instadeath to damage). -ekiM

[14]: Lavender(?) dragons with a paralysis attack. Lavender Scale Mail
provides free action. -ekiM

[15]: The Whiter than White dragon. Breaths bolts of lightening, which
blanks scrolls, and makes potions milky. Wearing this DSM reduces
dexterity by 3 (you can't dance) -SpeedEvil

[16]: Shimmering dragon with a confusion attack. Wearing shimmering
dragon scale mail grants displacement. -ekiM

